<!-- ====== SLIDE 4: The Eureka — Walking the Dog ====== -->
<section class="slide dark" id="s4">
  <span class="logo">&lt;mdp&gt;</span>
  <span class="section-num">03</span>

  <!-- Eureka marker -->
  <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.3); border-radius: 100px; padding: 0.4rem 1.2rem 0.4rem 0.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
    <span style="font-size: 1.4rem;">💡</span>
    <span style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);">Eureka Moment</span>
  </div>

  <h2>A walk, a podcast, and a reframe</h2>

  <div style="max-width: 800px; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 2rem; align-items: flex-start;">
      <div style="font-size: 3rem; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.25rem;">🐕</div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #BBBBBB;">
          This morning I was walking the dog, listening to Nathaniel Whittemore's
          <em>AI Daily Brief</em> podcast. He made a distinction that stopped me on the sidewalk:
        </p>

        <div class="pull-quote" style="margin: 2rem 0; color: var(--text-light);">
          Most companies are using AI for <strong style="color: var(--accent);">efficiency</strong> —
          doing existing things faster.<br>
          The real unlock is AI as <strong style="color: var(--accent);">opportunity</strong> —
          doing things that weren't possible before.
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #BBBBBB;">
          And I realized: <span style="color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500;">that's exactly where FCM Companion is right now.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem; display: flex; gap: 2rem; max-width: 800px;">
    <div style="flex: 1; padding: 1.5rem; background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.08); border-radius: 10px; border-left: 4px solid #EF4444;">
      <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: #FCA5A5; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Where we are</p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #FECACA;">
        AI does the work behind the scenes. Generates cases, gives feedback. The student never sees it.
        It's a faster version of what already exists.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; padding: 1.5rem; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.08); border-radius: 10px; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);">
      <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: #6EE7B7; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Where we could go</p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #A7F3D0;">
        AI is visible. Students learn to work <em>with</em> it — prompting, evaluating, critiquing clinical reasoning.
        FCM Companion becomes how UVA teaches M1s to practice medicine with AI.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p style="margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; font-style: italic;">
    Nathaniel Whittemore, <em>AI Daily Brief / Superintelligent</em> — "AI efficiency vs. AI opportunity"
  </p>
</section>

<!-- ====== SLIDE 5: The Shift ====== -->
<section class="slide" id="s5">
  <span class="logo">&lt;mdp&gt;</span>
  <span class="section-num">04</span>
  <div class="label">The Big Idea</div>
  <h2>AI Efficiency → AI Opportunity</h2>

  <div class="two-col" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
    <div>
      <span class="compare-label before">Current path</span>
      <h3>AI Efficiency</h3>
      <p class="subtitle" style="font-size: 1rem;">
        "Do your existing FCM prep faster with AI under the hood."
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;">
        Generates practice cases. Gives feedback on differentials. Creates a portal.
        Valuable — but incremental. Any study app could bolt this on.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="compare-label after">The opportunity</span>
      <h3>AI Opportunity</h3>
      <p class="subtitle" style="font-size: 1rem;">
        "Teach first-year medical students to <em>work with</em> generative AI through clinical content."
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem;">
        The AI isn't hidden — it's a visible co-pilot. Students see reasoning chains,
        learn to prompt, critique clinical AI thinking. The learning objective shifts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ====== SLIDE 6: What This Looks Like ====== -->
<section class="slide dark" id="s6">
  <span class="logo">&lt;mdp&gt;</span>
  <span class="section-num">05</span>
  <div class="label">AI Opportunity — In Practice</div>
  <h2>What this unlocks in FCM Companion</h2>

  <div class="cards" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon">🔍</div>
      <h3>"Show Your Work" Mode</h3>
      <p>AI's reasoning chain is visible. Students learn to spot where it's strong vs. where it hallucinates. Clinical AI literacy, not just clinical knowledge.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon">🎯</div>
      <h3>Prompted Practice</h3>
      <p>Structured exercises: "Ask the AI this three different ways — notice how the differential changes." Teaching prompting through clinical scenarios.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon">📊</div>
      <h3>AI Research Mode</h3>
      <p>Students combine patient data with literature search. Practice evaluating AI-generated clinical evidence. Learn when to trust, when to verify.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon">👩‍🏫</div>
      <h3>Instructor Dashboard</h3>
      <p>Faculty see how students interact with AI — not just case answers. A new feedback loop that doesn't exist in current FCM.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ====== SLIDE 7: The Meta ====== -->
<section class="slide" id="s7">
  <span class="logo">&lt;mdp&gt;</span>
  <span class="section-num">06</span>
  <div class="label">Why This Matters</div>
  <div class="pull-quote">
    You learned AI by building with it.<br>
    Now you're building something that teaches <em>others</em> to work with AI.<br>
    <span style="color: var(--accent);">That's the meta.</span>
  </div>
  <p class="subtitle" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
    FCM Companion stops being "a study app" and becomes the vehicle through which
    UVA introduces first-year medical students to generative AI in clinical contexts.
    That's a pitch the provost's office wants to see.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- ====== SLIDE 8: Guest — Justin Massa ====== -->
<section class="slide dark" id="s8">
  <span class="logo">&lt;mdp&gt;</span>
  <span class="section-num">07</span>
  <div class="label">10:00 – 11:00 AM</div>
  <h2>Justin Massa</h2>
  <p class="subtitle" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Partner & Co-Founder, Remix Partners</p>
  <p style="color: #777; font-size: 0.9rem;">Former IDEO. Helping companies build reliable AI systems.</p>

  <div class="cards" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); margin-top: 2rem;">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Jigs</h3>
      <p>The gap between "it worked when I showed it" and "it works every time." Frameworks for hardening AI workflows from demo to reproducible system.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Your Challenge</h3>
      <p>Identify one workflow in your feature area that needs to be a jig — something that must work reliably every time, not just in demo conditions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="question-list" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
    <li>
      <span class="q-number">?</span>
      <span>What's the most fragile part of FCM Companion right now — the thing that works in demo but would break for 100 M1 students?</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="q-number">?</span>
      <span>When you build a feature this week, how do you know it's reliable enough to merge back into the shared product?</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<!-- ====== SLIDE 9: Fork-Explore-Merge ====== -->
<section class="slide dark" id="s9">
  <span class="logo">&lt;mdp&gt;</span>
  <span class="section-num">08</span>
  <div class="label">Week 2 Workflow</div>
  <h2>Fork → Explore → Merge</h2>
  <p class="subtitle">
    You're a product team now. Each person owns a feature direction.
    Go deep individually, bring it back to the shared product.
  </p>

  <div class="flow" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
